Article27a
Access to energy, electricity networks and industrial self-consumption for industrial acceleration areas
1. Before an industrial acceleration area is designated or a strategic project is approved, the competent authorities shall carry out an energy and network assessment covering at least:
(a) the available electricity network capacity;
(b) any reinforcement required to the transmission and distribution networks;
(c) binding time limits for connection to the electricity network;
(d) the feasibility of individual and collective industrial self-consumption;
(e) access to shared energy storage facilities;
(f) the availability of bilateral renewable power purchase agreements for industrial undertakings;
(g) the establishment of industrial energy communities within industrial parks;
(h) coordination arrangements between the competent public authorities, transmission and distribution system operators, electricity suppliers and industrial operators; and
(i) the appointment of a regional energy coordinator, who shall cooperate with the coordinator responsible for strategic projects.
2. Member States shall ensure that projects located in industrial acceleration areas benefit from a dedicated and streamlined procedure for connection to the electricity network; individual and collective self-consumption installations; and energy storage facilities, including battery storage.

