ANNEX -I
Strategic sectors
1. Energy-intensive industries:
(a) Manufacture of basic iron and steel and of ferro-alloys, as classified under NACE Code 24.1;
(b) Manufacture of articles of concrete, cement and plaster, as classified under NACE Code 23.6;
(c) Manufacture of basic precious and other non-ferrous metals, including aluminium, as classified under NACE Code 24.4;
(d) Casting of metals, as classified under NACE Code 24.5;
(e) Manufacture of rubber and plastic products, as classified under NACE Code C22;
(f) Manufacture of glass and glass products, as classified under NACE Code 23.1;
(g) Manufacture of chemicals and chemicals products, as classified under NACE Code C20.
2. Automotive industry: manufacture of motor vehicles, trailers and semi-trailers, as classified under NACE Code C29;
3. Maritime industry: new shipbuilding, ship repair, ship maintenance and maritime equipment manufacturing activities as classified under NACE Code C30.1 - Building of ships and boats; C30.1.1 - Building of ships and floating structure; C33.1.5 - Repair and maintenance of ships and boats.

–for schemes established or updated on or after 1 January 2029 that benefit households or companies and that primarily aim to support the lease and purchase of motor vehicles for civil purposes, or support investments in the rail and maritime sectors, Member States, regional or local authorities, bodies governed by public law or associations formed by one or more such authorities or one or more such bodies governed by public law, shall ensure that only beneficiaries that comply with the following minimum requirements, are eligible:
(a) steel intended for use in motor vehicles for civil purposes: at least 25% of the total mass of steel used shall be low-carbon and of EU origin;
